#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# catalan_number

#% text
# `catalan_number(n)` gives the Catalan number `binomial(2*n, n)/(n + 1)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Catalan numbers count, among other things, the ways to bracket a product of `n + 1` factors and the binary trees with `n` nodes.

#% item
# Integer `n >= 0` gives integers of any size; `catalan_number` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
catalan_number(5)
#% output
#= 42

#% cell
catalan_number(0)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
catalan_number(range(10))
#% output
#= [1, 2, 5, 14, 42, 132, 429, 1430, 4862, 16796]

#% cell
catalan_number(100)
#% output
#= 896519947090131496687170070074100632420837521538745909320

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The binomial form:

#% cell
[catalan_number(12), binomial(24, 12)/13]
#% output
#= [208012, 208012]

#% text
# The recurrence `C(n + 1)` as the sum of `C(k)*C(n - k)`:

#% cell
[catalan_number(8), sum(catalan_number(k)*catalan_number(7 - k), [k, 0, 7])]
#% output
#= [1430, 1430]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `binomial`, `catalan`, `stirling_s2`, `partitions_p`
